  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S Milk Food Ltd vs State on 1 March, 2021",
    "facts": "The Laboratory examined the sample and issued a report dated 07.09.2011 wherein, a totally laconic opinion has been expressed that the sample does M/S Milk Food Ltd vs State on 1 March, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/158266885/ 1 not conform to Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955 as per tests performed.",
    "arguments": "The fervent contention of learned counsel Shri Jain is that the sample of the food article (dairy creamer) does not violate the standards prescribed in the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules and the appendices thereto. He urges that the learned ACJM, while considering the aspect of framing of charges, failed to refer to the report of the CFL and thus, the impugned order is bad in the eyes of law and same deserves to be [LEAKAGE_MASK] and [LEAKAGE_MASK]. Learned Public Prosecutor, on the other hand, submits that CFL report might have escaped the notice of the court but this cannot be a ground to discharge the accused because in the CFL report also, it has been mentioned that the sample did not conform to the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955. Nonetheless, learned Public Prosecutor is not in a position to dispute the fact that CFL report does not mention as to which particular clause of the Rules was being violated on the basis of the analyais carried out.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The fervent contention of learned counsel Shri Jain is that the sample of the food article (dairy creamer) does not violate the standards prescribed in the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules and the appendices thereto. He urges that the learned ACJM, while considering the aspect of framing of charges, failed to refer to the report of the CFL and thus, the impugned order is bad in the eyes of law and same deserves to be [LEAKAGE_MASK] and [LEAKAGE_MASK]. Learned Public Prosecutor, on the other hand, submits that CFL report might have escaped the notice of the court but this cannot be a ground to discharge the accused because in the CFL report also, it has been mentioned that the sample did not conform to the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955. Nonetheless, learned Public Prosecutor is not in a position to dispute the fact that CFL report does not mention as to which particular clause of the Rules was being violated on the basis of the analyais carried out.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
